From fa836c250649fb67d37eac324747074a49cedff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EdgePace authors <edgepace@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] EdgePace: sliding-window scheduler, fine graph cutting,
 external rho policy

- ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp, ggml/src/ggml-edgepace.h, ggml/src/edgepace/abi.h,
  ggml/src/edgepace_policy_abi.h: the scheduler submits each graph as quanta cut at
  legal boundaries (Fine Plan maps: text prefill/decode layers, vision encoder layers)
  through a sliding window of outstanding quanta; an external policy decides per
  quantum (window 2 / 1 / 0) from the application's task, progress and PMU signal
  pages and the request page.
- external/edgepace_policy: the policy DSO (libedgepace_policy.so): profile_static for
  Fine Plan timing, the rho policy rho = wD D + wS S + wU U with U = 1 - L / H,
  L = (d - t) - (1 + k) W_fg (EDGEPACE_RHO_*), freshness rescue.
- ggml/src/predictor: the application progress predictor (shared with the sampler).
